        "create_time": 1778826421.381,
        "update_time": 1778826439.383221,
        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "翻译：\"\" Feature-Space Cross-Check for the AFIB Discovery Case\r\n[Supplementary]: Feature-group permutation importance on\r\nXGBoost Clinical-MVP confirms that AV Conduction Timing\r\nfeatures dominate AFIB detection (∆AUROC= 0.179 [0.171,\r\n0.188]), exceeding Rhythm & Rate features (∆AUROC=\r\n0.077; Supplementary Table S7). This complements the\r\nResNet perturbation results with an important methodological\r\npoint: different model classes emphasize overlapping but non\r\nidentical information channels, so single-model auditing risks\r\nover-interpretation.\"\""
          ]
        },
